# v1465 — per-install identity: unique per PC, must NEVER travel between machines
# v2119 — AND THE ROOT COPIES. These two patterns name `tv/` only, so `git check-ignore` was
# silent on `/.tvd_identity.json` and `git add -A` staged it into a PUBLIC repo, carrying this
# machine's install id, its hostname and its username. Anyone cloning inherited konyo-3.local's
# identity as their own. [[the-unjoined-end]]
/.tvd_identity.json
/.tvd_beacon.json
tv/.tvd_identity.json

# v2146 — WHICH WORLD THE BOARD CAME BACK AS. Same class as .tvd_identity.json directly above, and
# nearly the same near-miss: v2145 added this file and did NOT ignore it, so the first time the
# console wrote it a `git add -A` would have staged a per-install identity into a PUBLIC repo — the
# exact thing the note above records happening once already. Caught by a cross-family review before
# the file was ever written. The .tmp is the atomic-write partner and must go too.
tv/.board_identity.json
tv/.board_identity.json.tmp
# v1597 — the beacon's own last-result record. Per-install and machine-specific (attempts,
# failures, the IP-dependent verdict), exactly like .tvd_identity.json beside it. Committing
# it would push one machine's beacon history onto every other machine that pulls.
tv/.tvd_beacon.json

