_ls*.html
_lsfork_probe.html

# v1481 — runtime state the launcher writes, not source. start_tvd_win.ps1 caches the
# "webview imports cleanly" probe result here so every launch does not re-pay it; the value is
# true for THIS machine's python only, so committing it would hand another machine a stale answer
# about an interpreter it does not have.
tv/.webview_ok
_freshpc_probe.html
_sigil_probe.html
_worlds_probe.html
# v1524 — per-machine sweep memory: which sealed reels the Chronicle sweep has already read.
# Machine-local by nature (his Mac and the Windows cousin have different footage) and worthless
# to anyone else, so it never travels.
tv/chronicle_swept.json
# v2184 — the hunt's memory of which PAID hunts came back empty. Same reason as the line above:
# it is live state, it names items off his own reels, and this repo is PUBLIC. I created it in
# v2174 and did not add it here, so `git add -A` swept the running console's copy into a public
# commit within hours. Every path in run_gates._LIVE_STATE is now required to be ignored, by a
# test, because remembering is not a mechanism.
tv/chron_hunt_memory.json
tv/auto_relaunch.json
# v2189 — the board's own tally, handed over by bible.html so the fleet numbers work on Windows
# too. Live state, and it names his progress: never committed to a PUBLIC repo.
tv/board_tally.json
tv/shadow_ledger.json
tv/.render_shots/

# v1711 — the G5 stats ledger is per-machine runtime counters, like the budget file
tv/g5_stats.json

# v1777 — the accumulated sighting ledger is LIVE MACHINE STATE, not source. It is rewritten
