# v2394 — the eagle's durable pass. A RUNTIME DECISION RECORD, like .second_eye.jsonl and
# .console_scars.json: his running console rewrites it every pass, so tracking it leaves the
# working tree permanently dirty and every pre-push reports "local tracked edits present".
tv/.eagle_last.json
# v2454 — CF-8 unknown-age + CF-12 last slow pass. Runtime, per-machine, never committed.
tv/.unknown_age.json
tv/.unknown_age.json.tmp
tv/.eagle_slow.json
tv/.eagle_slow.json.tmp
tv/.unknown_age.scratch-*.json
tv/.eagle_slow.scratch-*.json
# ⚠ v2413 — AND EVERY SCRATCH VARIANT OF IT. v2411 routed the eagle record through _decision_path
# so a scratch console writes `<stem>.scratch-<port><ext>` instead of clobbering the primary's
# file. That was the right fix and it minted a filename this list did not match — so
# tv/.eagle_last.scratch-17985.json was TRACKED and committed to a PUBLIC repo, and would churn on
# every pass of every scratch console, on both his machines.
# A new path pattern needs a new ignore in the same breath; the isolation and the ignore are two
# halves of one change. [[the-unjoined-end]]
tv/.eagle_last.scratch-*.json
# ⚠ AND THE SWEEP FOUND THE SAME GAP ALREADY THERE, PREDATING MY CHANGE. `_decision_path` has two
# consumers; auto_relaunch.json was the original and its scratch form was never ignored either. It
# happens not to exist on disk today, which is why nobody noticed — an absent file and a covered
# one look identical in `git status`. Fixing the CLASS rather than the instance I introduced.
# [[sweep-dont-ask]]
tv/auto_relaunch.scratch-*.json
# ⚠ v2428 — THIRD TIME, SO STOP LISTING INSTANCES AND COVER THE SHAPE. Routing ui_faults.jsonl
# through the same primary/scratch split minted `tv/ui_faults.scratch-17791.jsonl`, and the note
# six lines up — written when exactly this happened at v2413 — did not prevent it, because it
# named two files rather than the pattern that generates them. `.scratch-<port>` is minted by
# construction for runtime DECISION records only; nothing under tv/ wearing that infix is ever
# meant to be tracked. [[sweep-dont-ask]] [[feedback-generalize-fixes]]
tv/*.scratch-*
tv/.*.scratch-*


